OL,3,GNEWSA'Incredible to hear my umbilical
OL,4,Acord saved a life'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA 30-year-old woman said it was
OL,7,F"incredible" to learn her donated
OL,8,Fumbilical cord was used by the NHS to
OL,9,Fsave a child's life in Australia.
OL,11,FJade Reed from St Albans,
OL,12,FHertfordshire, became the first person
OL,13,Fwhose stem cells were used for
OL,14,Femergency treatment via the NHS cord
OL,15,Fblood bank after it launched in 1996.
OL,17,FThe process is anonymous so the NHS was
OL,18,Funable to give full details of the
OL,19,Fbeneficiary - but to mark the blood
OL,20,Fbank's 30th anniversary, Jade and her
OL,21,Fmum were told their donation helped a
OL,22,Fchild with blood cancer.
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
